GIS & Mapping		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	

 
    
	  	  

	   

	   

			   
		 				
	 

	 	



 
	 

		 
			 Cora Van Hazinga, the Town’s GIS Coordinator, teams up with the Veterans Services Officer, Meg Murphy, to introduce Cub Scout Pack 1455 to the world of GIS—Geographic Information Systems, the digital tools that help us make maps and understand where things are—and GPS, the satellite-based system that tells us exactly where we are on Earth. During their hands-on adventure in Walton Cemetery, the scouts learned about the tools that are used to map final resting places of Veterans in the cemetery’s oldest sections, ensuring these heroes’ stories remain remembered for generations to come. 
		 
	 
 

 
	.widget .textContent p:first-child {
		padding-top: 0px;
		margin-top: 0px;
	}

 


	   

	   

			   
		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         What is GIS? GIS is a technology used to create, manage, analyze, and map all types of data. GIS is a powerful tool for municipalities- it can help local government optimize planning, enhance emergency response, support public works, manage town assets, and improve environmental management. GIS also plays an important part in transparent government by making important information (ranging from tax parcels to flood zones) easily accessible to residents.  If you have any questions about GIS or requests for maps, please don't hesitate to reach out to the Pepperell GIS Department. Available Maps Property Information/Tax Parcels For the most up-to-date property information, visit the  Public Web Map .  Detailed  Assessors Maps  are updated annually for the most recently closed fiscal tax year.  Parcels are continually being updated for accuracy and new development. Not all parcels have been verified for accuracy, and not all easements, rights-of-way, or other legal constraints may appear on the map. Although the Town can provide approximate locations of rights-of-way and public utility easements, we cannot verify parcel boundaries or resolve private land disputes. To research deeds and plot plans, which represent record of legal ownership, visit the  Registry of Deeds . Pepperell Conservation Areas and Trail Map Check out our newly published  Pepperell Conservation Areas and Trail Map , created in cooperation with  Nashoba Conservation Trust . This interactive map, available on desktop and mobile, displays all public open space and trails in Pepperell. Use filters to find trails popular with horse riders, mountain bikers, and cross country skiers, as well as more accessibly-designed hiking trails.   Pepperell Street Map The  Pepperell Street Map  contains information on public and private ways in town. Other GIS Resources MassMapper Mass GeoDOT 
     

 
